A||N||6||AusFiero||Performance Advise Sought. 2.8 V6 , Brakes, Suspension????||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||09-19-2001||08:06 AM||||Well I am in the process of rebuilding the crisped 86 and as much as I would like to put a SC 3.8 I can't really justify the expense. Costs about $10,000 to do here. I will talk in US dollars from here on to make it easier for yous.<P>So what can be done to make a 2.8 perform bearing in mind a US$3000 budget (approx). I can get an Eaton supercharger new for $600, is this worth using. What can be done to beef up the internals and perhaps increase the engine displacement.<P>Brake wise what can be done with a $1500 (approx) budget? <P>Suspension now and what can be done with a $1500 budget also. All these amounts are approximate. <P>I have decided to stay with the 2.8 because I have 6 weeks to build this car or it will start costing me storage money. Also I have so many new sensors and other bits on the engine including the whole clutch system being new that I figured why waste money on more new stuff when the car is for show more than go. <P>All up I have a budget of about US$11,000 to throw at the car, bearing in mind some of this is going to get eaten by grit blasting, new paint, new interior and shipping parts from the USA. <P>So throw your ideas at me everyone, please. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-19-2001||08:28 AM||||Drop in a 3.4 iron head pushrod engine - all your sensors and brackets fit. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-19-2001||12:15 PM||||Aus... For $1500 Brake budget , buy archies 11.25" vented kit. I didn't buy his kit, but I have the same setup and it is AMAZING!! well worth the hassle to buy a completed kit too. perhaps you could barter for some of your body panels??<P>As for the suspension , Koni's for the front and rear , and your choice of lowering springs.<P>As for the motor ...I would get a 3.4ltr long block from ed parks. Not the most power for the money , you could throw a turbo on the 2.8 for $3000 , but the 3.4 is a newer stonger motor , that would be a good base for a future turbo /supercharger project.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||09-19-2001||12:36 PM||||AUS-<P>I agree with Slammed-<P>Go with Archie's brakes... I wantemtoo!<P>Get ahold of 3.4 Pushrod motor, bolt on the Fiero top end, maybe get a bored-out TB and Intake plenum from Darrell Morse (+13% airflow). Also do a port & polish on the heads if you can, and be sure to port the stock exhaust manifolds...that'll pick up a few HP right off!<P>Suspension- Koni adjustables all around and some good lowering springs (eibachs are good).<P>Keep us updated on your project/projects! Hope the rebuild it going well.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroGTguy||09-19-2001||01:20 PM||||I have an RCC 12" Corvette brake kit for sale, and it has less than 1000 miles on it.  Probably only a few hundred.<P>The Corvette calipers have a dual piston along with the larger rotor.<P>The kit is $1800 from RCC.<P>For $800 + shipping, I'd let you have everything.<P>- New from hub + bearings<BR>- New front and rear caliper brackets<BR>- Calipers and rotors all the way around<P>I think that it's the most brake for the buck.  The reason I am selling is that I am going with held's 12" quad piston caliper and brake set-up.<P>Let me know if you are interested.  I will also consider partial trades for side scoops, or maybe even credit for that stage 2 kit.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  How is that coming?<P>Greg||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||09-19-2001||01:44 PM||||Jim,<P>call George at Fiero Shop ... he can explain the '88 style suspension and brake upgrade he is working on .. you might like it ($ wise...) 866-343-7648 (toll free) or 510-233-4376||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||09-19-2001||09:27 PM|||| The easiest thing to do would be to increase the volumetric efficiency of the 2.8 you have. You could do this by,<BR>*Porting the restrictions from the stock exhaust manifolds <BR>*Have a performance valve job done on the heads and fit the heads with SI valves, and stiffer springs<BR>*Higher flow exhaust<BR>*Underdrive pulley<BR>*Turbocharger<BR>*K$N filter<BR>*Performance camshaft like Cran Powermax H-260-2<BR>*The usual hot rod items<P>I wouldn't mess with the bottom end if the mileage is low and the motor is in good running condition. Just look at what 1FAST2M6 got for power from his fist 2.8 car without the nitrous. I think he had 150-160 RWH or something like that.  <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
